ature to lower temperature"}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:physics:thermodynamics:3", "question_text": "At constant pressure, heat supplied to a system equals the change in what quantity?", "options": ["Entropy", "Momentum", "Enthalpy", "Resistance"], "correct_answer": 2, "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "At constant pressure, q equals delta H"}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:physics:thermodynamics:4", "question_text": "Which equation represents the first law of thermodynamics?", "options": ["Q = U - W", "Q = P/V", "Q = mc", "Q = U + W"], "correct_answer": 3, "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "With this sign convention, heat added equals internal energy change plus work done"}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:physics:thermodynamics:5", "question_text": "Absolute zero is equal to which temperature?", "options": ["0 C", "0 K", "-100 C", "273 K"], "correct_answer": 1, "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Absolute zero is 0 kelvin"}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:physics:thermodynamics:6", "question_text": "What remains constant in an isothermal process?", "options": ["Pressure", "Volume", "Temperature", "Mass density"], "correct_answer": 2, "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Isothermal means constant temperature"}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:physics:thermodynamics:7", "question_text": "The efficiency of an ideal Carnot engine depends on what?", "options": ["Only working substance mass", "Only pressure", "Only volume", "Only reservoir temperatures"], "correct_answer": 3, "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Carnot efficiency is determined by hot and cold reservoir temperatures"}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:physics:thermodynamics:8", "question_text": "In an adiabatic process, the heat transfer Q is what?", "options": ["Zero", "Positive", "Negative", "Maximum"], "correct_answer": 0, "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "No heat is exchanged in an adiabatic process"}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:physics:thermodynamics:9", "question_text": "For an ideal gas, internal energy depends primarily on what?", "options": ["Pressure only", "Volume only", "Temperature only", "Number of moles only"], "correct_answer": 2, "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "Internal energy of an ideal gas is a function of temperature"}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:physics:thermodynamics:10", "question_text": "According to the second law, what happens to the entropy of an isolated system?", "options": ["It always decreases", "It never decreases", "It always stays zero", "It alternates"], "correct_answer": 1, "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "Entropy does not decrease for spontaneous change in an isolated system"}]}, {"name": "Optics", "slug": "optics", "questions": [{"seed_key": "demo:question:physics:optics:1", "question_text": "Parallel rays incident on a convex lens meet at which point?", "options": ["Principal focus", "Center of curvature", "Optical center only", "Pole"], "correct_answer": 0, "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "A convex lens converges parallel rays to its focus"}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:physics:optics:2", "question_text": "What is the unit of lens power?", "options": ["Metre", "Dioptre", "Candela", "Tesla"], "correct_answer": 1, "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Lens power is measured in dioptres"}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:physics:optics:3", "question_text": "In reflection, the angle of reflection is equal to what?", "options": ["Angle of deviation", "Angle of refraction", "Angle of incidence", "Angle of polarization"], "correct_answer": 2, "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "The law of reflection makes these angles equal"}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:physics:optics:4", "question_text": "A real image formed by a concave mirror can be what?", "options": ["Seen only in a microscope", "Always upright", "Always virtual", "Formed on a screen"], "correct_answer": 3, "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Real images can be projected"}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:physics:optics:5", "question_text": "Refractive index of a medium is equal to which ratio?", "options": ["speed in medium / speed in vacuum", "speed in vacuum / speed in medium", "wavelength in vacuum / frequency", "frequency / wavelength"], "correct_answer": 1, "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The refractive index n equals c divided by v"}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:physics:optics:6", "question_text": "A rainbow is produced mainly due to what effects?", "options": ["Diffraction only", "Reflection only", "Dispersion and internal reflection", "Interference only"], "correct_answer": 2, "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Raindrops disperse and internally reflect light"}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:physics:optics:7", "question_text": "In myopia, the image of distant objects forms where?", "options": ["Behind the retina", "On the retina", "On the cornea", "Before the retina"], "correct_answer": 3, "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Short-sightedness forms the image before the retina"}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:physics:optics:8", "question_text": "What is the power of a lens of focal length 20 cm?", "options": ["5 D", "2 D", "4 D", "10 D"], "correct_answer": 0, "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "Power is the reciprocal of focal length in metres"}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:physics:optics:9", "question_text": "What is the magnification of a plane mirror?", "options": ["0", "2", "1", "It varies with distance"], "correct_answer": 2, "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "A plane mirror forms an image of equal size"}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:physics:optics:10", "question_text": "In Young's double-slit experiment, a bright fringe occurs when path difference is what?", "options": ["(2n + 1)lambda/2", "n lambda", "lambda/4", "Zero only"], "correct_answer": 1, "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "Constructive interference occurs for integer multiples of lambda"}]}, {"name": "Electricity and Magnetism", "slug": "electricity_and_magnetism", "questions": [{"seed_key": "demo:question:physics:electricity_and_magnetism:1", "question_text": "What is the SI unit of electric current?", "options": ["Ampere", "Volt", "Ohm", "Coulomb"], "correct_answer": 0, "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Current is measured in amperes"}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:physics:electricity_and_magnetism:2", "question_text": "Ohm's law is written as which equation?", "options": ["P = VI", "V = IR", "Q = It", "F = qE"], "correct_answer": 1, "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Ohm's law relates voltage, current, and resistance"}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:physics:electricity_and_magnetism:3", "question_text": "What is the charge on an electron?", "options": ["Positive", "Neutral", "Negative", "Variable"], "correct_answer": 2, "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "An electron carries negative elementary charge"}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:physics:electricity_and_magnetism:4", "question_text": "In a series circuit, which quantity is the same through each component?", "options": ["Voltage", "Charge stored", "Resistance", "Current"], "correct_answer": 3, "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Series components share the same current"}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:physics:electricity_and_magnetism:5", "question_text": "Electric power is given by which expression?", "options": ["P = IR", "P = VI", "P = V/R", "P = Q/t^2"], "correct_answer": 1, "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Power equals voltage times current"}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:physics:electricity_and_magnetism:6", "question_text": "What shape are the magnetic field lines around a long straight current-carrying wire?", "options": ["Straight radial lines", "Parabolas", "Concentric circles", "Ellipses"], "correct_answer": 2, "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "The field wraps around the wire"}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:physics:electricity_and_magnetism:7", "question_text": "A capacitor is primarily used to store what?", "options": ["Magnetic flux", "Heat", "Mechanical energy", "Electric charge"], "correct_answer