ighted graph."}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:data_structures_and_algorithms:trees_and_graphs:8", "question_text": "Which term best matches this description: it grows on the order of log n?", "options": ["Balanced BST height", "Topological sort", "Spanning tree", "Binary tree"], "correct_answer": 0, "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "Balanced BST height fits because it grows on the order of log n."}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:data_structures_and_algorithms:trees_and_graphs:9", "question_text": "Which term best matches this description: it is defined only for directed acyclic graphs?", "options": ["Spanning tree", "Binary tree", "Topological sort", "Root"], "correct_answer": 2, "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "Topological sort fits because it is defined only for directed acyclic graphs."}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:data_structures_and_algorithms:trees_and_graphs:10", "question_text": "Which term best matches this description: it connects n vertices using exactly n - 1 edges?", "options": ["Binary tree", "Spanning tree", "Root", "Leaf"], "correct_answer": 1, "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "Spanning tree fits because it connects n vertices using exactly n - 1 edges."}]}, {"name": "Searching and Sorting", "slug": "searching_and_sorting", "questions": [{"seed_key": "demo:question:data_structures_and_algorithms:searching_and_sorting:1", "question_text": "Which term best matches this description: it scans elements sequentially to find a target?", "options": ["Linear search", "Binary search", "Bubble sort", "Merge sort"], "correct_answer": 0, "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Linear search fits because it scans elements sequentially to find a target."}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:data_structures_and_algorithms:searching_and_sorting:2", "question_text": "Which term best matches this description: it requires data to be sorted before halving the search space?", "options": ["Bubble sort", "Binary search", "Merge sort", "Average O(n log n) quicksort"], "cor