ion", "Turnaround time", "Shortest job first", "Waiting time"], "correct_answer": 2, "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Shortest job first fits because it chooses the process with the smallest cpu burst time."}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:operating_systems:cpu_scheduling:4", "question_text": "Which term best matches this description: it allows the scheduler to interrupt a running process?", "options": ["Turnaround time", "Waiting time", "Context-switch overhead", "Preemption"], "correct_answer": 3, "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Preemption fits because it allows the scheduler to interrupt a running process."}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:operating_systems:cpu_scheduling:5", "question_text": "Which term best matches this description: it measures time from submission to completion?", "options": ["Waiting time", "Turnaround time", "Context-switch overhead", "Aging"], "correct_answer": 1, "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Turnaround time fits because it measures time from submission to completion."}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:operating_systems:cpu_scheduling:6", "question_text": "Which term best matches this description: it measures how long a process spends in the ready queue?", "options": ["Context-switch overhead", "Aging", "Waiting time", "Throughput"], "correct_answer": 2, "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Waiting time fits because it measures how long a process spends in the ready queue."}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:operating_systems:cpu_scheduling:7", "question_text": "Which term best matches this description: it rises when the time quantum becomes very small?", "options": ["Aging", "Throughput", "Multilevel feedback queue", "Context-switch overhead"], "correct_answer": 3, "difficulty": "medium", "explanation": "Context-switch overhead fits because it rises when the time quantum becomes very small."}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:operating_systems:cpu_scheduling:8", "question_text": "Which term best matches this description: it can reduce starvation in priority scheduling?", "options": ["Aging", "Throughput", "Multilevel feedback queue", "FCFS scheduling"], "correct_answer": 0, "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "Aging fits because it can reduce starvation in priority scheduling."}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:operating_systems:cpu_scheduling:9", "question_text": "Which term best matches this description: it counts the number of completed processes per unit time?", "options": ["Multilevel feedback queue", "FCFS scheduling", "Throughput", "Round robin"], "correct_answer": 2, "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "Throughput fits because it counts the number of completed processes per unit time."}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:operating_systems:cpu_scheduling:10", "question_text": "Which term best matches this description: it adapts scheduling priority based on observed behavior?", "options": ["FCFS scheduling", "Multilevel feedback queue", "Round robin", "Shortest job first"], "correct_answer": 1, "difficulty": "hard", "explanation": "Multilevel feedback queue fits because it adapts scheduling priority based on observed behavior."}]}, {"name": "Deadlocks", "slug": "deadlocks", "questions": [{"seed_key": "demo:question:operating_systems:deadlocks:1", "question_text": "Which term best matches this description: it is a state where processes wait forever for resources held by each other?", "options": ["Deadlock", "Mutual exclusion", "Hold and wait", "Circular wait"], "correct_answer": 0, "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Deadlock fits because it is a state where processes wait forever for resources held by each other."}, {"seed_key": "demo:question:operating_systems:deadlocks:2", "question_text": "Which term best matches this description: it is one of the Coffman conditions for deadlock?", "options": ["Hold and wait", "Mutual exclusion", "Circular wait", "Safe state"], "correct_answer": 1, "difficulty": "easy", "explanation": "Mutual exclusion fits because it is one of the coffman conditions for d